Model versioning	MODEL_VERSION = "v1.0" stored in every prediction record
What is NOT there (genuine gaps):

No trained model files — the .pkl files don't exist yet. You need to run python scripts/train_models.py against your dataset first. Until then, the system falls back to a rule-based scoring formula (implemented, not ideal).
No time-window / rolling features — the document mentions "time-window/statistical features" (Step 19). What's built is single-reading feature engineering. Rolling mean, rolling std, trend over the last N readings is not implemented.
No multi-class failure classification — the failure model is binary (0=normal, 1=failure). Multi-class (bearing failure vs thermal overload vs imbalance) would need labeled multi-class training data.
No model retraining API — there's no endpoint to trigger retraining from accumulated DB data. Currently only 
train_models.py
 does it.
RAG — Status: Fully Implemented, Externally Dependent
Every stage of Section 17's pipeline is implemented end-to-end.

What is fully done:

Component	What's there
loader.py	PDF (pypdf, page-by-page), DOCX (python-docx, paragraph extraction), TXT, directory batch loading
chunker.py	Character-based overlapping chunking with sentence boundary detection, whitespace normalisation, token estimation
embeddings.py	OpenAI text-embedding-3-small (1536 dims), batched API calls (100 per batch), retry logic (3 attempts, exponential backoff), zero-vector fallback when no API key
retriever.py	pgvector cosine similarity search using <=> operator + ivfflat index, keyword ILIKE fallback when pgvector unavailable, doc_type filter, relevance scoring
pipeline.py	Full orchestration: load → chunk → batch embed → persist KnowledgeDocument + KnowledgeChunk records
ai_service.py	Grounded prompt construction (machine context + ML result + RAG chunks), OpenAI GPT-4o call, structured EXPLANATION/RECOMMENDATION parsing, token usage tracking, retry logic, placeholder when no API key
Knowledge search API	POST /api/knowledge/search — semantic search endpoint
Document ingest API	POST /api/knowledge/ingest — file upload endpoint (admin only)
What is NOT there (genuine gaps):

No documents ingested yet — data/knowledge/ is empty. The 6 documents from Section 17.1 (machine_manual.pdf, maintenance_sop.pdf, etc.) don't exist; you need to provide and ingest them.
No re-ranking — chunks are returned by raw cosine similarity. A cross-encoder re-ranker would improve quality but is not in the MVP scope.
No chunking by semantic units — chunking is character-based with sentence boundary snapping. Semantic/paragraph-aware chunking (e.g. LangChain's RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter with token-based splitting) would be more accurate but is a Week 5+ enhancement.
No retrieval quality evaluation — Step 43 of the document says "evaluate retrieval quality using sample questions". There's no automated retrieval evaluation harness.
Embedding quality depends on API key — without OPENAI_API_KEY, all embeddings are zero vectors. The keyword fallback works but is much weaker.
